summary:
  The larger view of the cover asks for the picture under an address of
  its own, and Qt fetches it again for that.

history:
  Qt keeps a decoded picture under its address, its size and its fill
  mode, and a second Image that differs in any of them gets no share of
  the first one's. The larger view was first written with
  PreserveAspectFit beside the cover's crop, and a server on the loopback
  counted two requests for one click. The cover and its larger view are
  one component now, so the address is the one thing left that can set
  them apart. This mutant gives the larger view one of its own.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CoverTouch.qml

find:
              source: touch.larger ? touch.art : ""

replace:
              source: touch.larger ? touch.art + "#larger" : ""

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cover_larger_fetch.py::test_the_larger_cover_is_the_picture_the_page_already_holds.
  Line-neutral.
